205	// startSessionPrefetch is the distill pipeline's producer: it prepares
206	// sessions in chronological order and dispatches their chunk agent calls into
207	// ONE shared pool, up to `concurrency` calls in flight ACROSS sessions — the
208	// per-session pool it replaces gave a 1-chunk session (the common case after
209	// stripping; the corpus median) no parallelism at all, serializing the run on
210	// agent latency.
211	//
212	// Two properties carry over from the per-session prefetcher and one is new:
213	//   - In-order delivery: the consumer applies chunks strictly in global
214	//     (session, chunk) order, so reconcile and fact application keep their
215	//     exact serial semantics; only agent round-trips overlap.
216	//   - Consumption-bounded lookahead: a pool slot is held from a call's launch
217	//     until its result is CONSUMED, so at most `concurrency` completed results
218	//     are ever buffered and an early abort stops dispatch within `concurrency`
219	//     calls of the last one consumed.
220	//   - Single dispatcher, global dispatch order: slots are acquired in exactly
221	//     the order the consumer will need results. Competing per-session
222	//     dispatchers over a shared pool could hand a freed slot to a session the
223	//     consumer is not ready for, buffering its result while the chunk the
224	//     consumer is blocked on starves — a deadlock at small pool sizes.
225	//
226	// The returned channel delivers sessions in order with lookahead
227	// distillSessionLookahead; it closes when all sessions are produced or ctx is
228	// canceled. Cancel ctx to stop preparation, dispatch, and in-flight calls.
229	func startSessionPrefetch(ctx context.Context, brainDir, repoDir string, args []string, sessions []exportSession, prevCache distillCache, distillOpts distillCommandOptions, resolveBranch func(exportSession) string) <-chan preparedSession {
